  2. d-04  Numerically read Figs. 12-13 of arXiv:2602.12303 for a galaxy-cluster keyword or subfield bar  -- The figures were extracted but never read and are the most direct 2025-specific source; a Fig. 13 sub-field count divided by 18,660 is a paper share
  3. d-09  Extract a sourced galaxy-cluster concept or topic share from AstroMLab 5 (arXiv:2511.12353) as an independent anchor for the within-astro-ph cluster fraction, ideally for recent years.  -- It is the only remaining plausible sourced anchor for the within-astro-ph cluster fraction
  4. d-05  Re-read and cite() the 18,660 total, cross-submission exclusion and Table 1 counts from arXiv:2602.12303  -- The stored excerpts were truncated, so the base numbers are not shown verbatim
  5. d-02  Independently derive the share of galaxy-cluster papers and the 2020-2025 trend from AstroMLab 5 (2511.12353) and other citable bibliometric sources, as a cross-check on d-01.  -- No per-year cluster data exists; only total-paper growth (+14.2%) is sourced, and the 2024 back-projection is non-independent
