[brief] No source we found gives a direct count of 2025 arXiv papers on galaxy cluster physics, so this has to be built from a total and a fraction. My rough estimate is about 1,000 to 1,500 papers where clus
**Survey** — 9 tools on 1 servers, 2 papers found.

No source we found gives a direct count of 2025 arXiv papers on galaxy cluster physics, so this has to be built from a total and a fraction. My rough estimate is about 1,000 to 1,500 papers where clusters (the intracluster medium, cluster cosmology, cluster lensing, radio relics and halos, brightest cluster galaxies, cluster mergers) are the main subject, with a central value near 1,200. If 'on galaxy clusters' is read broadly, to include any paper where clusters are an important tool or sample (for example, galaxies in cluster environments or lensed high-redshift sources behind clusters), the count is more like 2,000 to 3,000. The total comes from a lead: a quote in a web search result (not read at the source) says the Open Journal of Astrophysics published 213 papers in 2025, 'only just over 1%' of astro-ph submissions. That puts new astro-ph submissions in 2025 at roughly 17,000 to 20,000, and around 20,000 to 25,000 if cross-lists from other archives are counted. As a cross-check, the AstroMLab 5 dataset contains 408,590 astro-ph papers from 1992 through July 2025, which fits a recent rate of roughly 18,000 to 20,000 or more per year. For the fraction, I assumed from general knowledge, not from any source found here, that cluster-focused work makes up about 5 to 8% of astro-ph. It sits mainly in astro-ph.CO and astro-ph.GA, with some in astro-ph.HE. So roughly 0.06 x 19,000 gives about 1,100, and the uncertainty is about a factor of 1.5. 'Astrophysics Wrapped 2025' (arXiv:2602.12303) analyses keywords and subfields for every 2025 astro-ph paper and may give a better fraction, but only its abstract was available.

Quantities worth checking: Total new astro-ph submissions in 2025, with and without cross-lists (from arXiv's own per-category submission statistics or from 2602.12303); Share of 2025 astro-ph papers whose title or abstract contains 'galaxy cluster', 'cluster of galaxies', 'intracluster', 'ICM', 'Sunyaev-Zel'dovich' together with 'cluster', or 'brightest cluster galaxy'; Check that keyword matches are not picking up star cluster or globular cluster papers; Gap between a narrow count (clusters as the main topic) and a broad count (any mention of clusters); Growth from year to year (compare 2023 and 2024 counts from the same query) to check the 2025 figure.
